# Evidence: KSyntaxHighlighting 6.18.0 task #15161, HarmonyOS PC device.
# Gap check at origin/main b544378a4ea82b4959135eebb21f5e509eeebf91:
# E344 mentions Qt6/KF6+CTest but concerns test inventory, not runtime; 0
# graph/doc files match qt_version_tag plus "symbol not found". Draft E666 is
# a Qt5 ABI mismatch case, not this Qt6 runtime-selection failure (see the MD).
id:                     DRAFT-kf6-qt-ctest-private-runtime-scope
draft:                  true
contributor_id:         iKalous_OscarP
status:                 pending-editor-review
trigger_tool:           ctest
phase:                  testing
error_signature:        Error relocating .*_test: .*symbol not found|qt_version_tag: symbol not found
severity:               2
category:               ohos, cmake, runtime, linking, conan
match_keywords:         CTest, Qt6, KF6, Error relocating, symbol not found, LD_LIBRARY_PATH, private Conan home
title:                  Scope the private Qt runtime to KF6 CTest instead of trusting a bare shell rerun
root_cause: >
  A CMake/Conan build can link KF6 Qt Test executables against the private Qt6
  package and still run them against a different runtime search environment.
  Conan's recipe-scoped Environment does not persist into an unrelated SSH
  shell. On the OHOS device, rerunning the six built binaries with bare ctest
  then failed at relocation for Qt symbols; the same binaries all passed when
  the private Qt lib directory and build bin directory were supplied only to
  that test invocation. A bare rerun is not evidence of a source-test failure.
affected_scope: >
  CMake/CTest consumers of Qt6 or KF6 in a private Conan cache on HarmonyOS PC,
  especially when test executables load Qt plugins or other shared libraries.
verification_cmd: >
  In the same build tree, compare env -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH ctest --test-dir BUILD
  with LD_LIBRARY_PATH=BUILD/bin:QT_PACKAGE/lib ctest --test-dir BUILD -V.
  Case #15161: 0/6 with relocation errors versus 6/6 and 1038 Qt Test PASS
  records, 0 fail, 0 skip with the private runtime environment.
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           recipe-scoped-private-qt-runtime
rec_description: >
  Resolve the Qt package folder from Conan's dependency graph. Wrap CTest in
  a Conan Environment context that prepends its lib and plugin directories
  and the current build's shared-library directory; create task-local runtime
  aliases if the OHOS loader cannot follow package symlinks. Keep the environment
  scoped to the test command, and report CTest and inner Qt Test totals.
rec_command:            with runtime_env.vars(self).apply(): self.run("ctest --test-dir ... --output-on-failure")
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conanfile
forbid_1_pattern:       BUILD_TESTING=OFF|ctest.*--exclude-regex
forbid_1_reason:        Disabling tests hides a loader selection problem rather than fixing it.
forbid_1_consequence:   CI can report a green package without upstream coverage.
forbid_2_pattern:       export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=.*\.conan2.*;.*conan create
forbid_2_reason:        A global override can contaminate toolchain subprocesses and trigger the alias behavior documented in E505.
forbid_2_consequence:   Build tools may pick the wrong shared library or fail to load an alias.
principles:             R34, R51
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E019, E344, E505, E520, E537]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []
doc_file:               drafts/DRAFT-kf6-qt-ctest-private-runtime-scope.md
last_updated:           2026-10-15
source_event:           task #15161 forced device rebuild and controlled CTest rerun
authors:                iKalous_OscarP <iKalous_OscarP@noreply.gitcode.com>
source_pr:
source_commit:
metrics_success_count:  1
metrics_fail_count:     0
metrics_confidence:     1.0
metrics_last_used:      2026-10-15
